Z||000000||kslish||06-14-2001||11:19 PM||||Hey all,<P>The Birch Run Best Western is all booked up for the weekend of the Michigan Fiero show (July 13th-15th).  Guess I should have made my reservations sooner, but I wan't sure that I was going to attend until recently.  Anyone from that area know of a fairly cheap alternative hotel to stay at that is close to there?  <P>Thanks,<P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bluebottlejunky||06-15-2001||12:24 AM||||hmmm, I need to know too, any good place's?<P>------------------<BR>Hello, My name is Mike and I am addicted too fiero's...PLEASE dont help me.<BR>85'GT 4sp<BR>AIM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||4
Z||000002||kslish||06-16-2001||05:46 AM||||Well, made some phone calls and browsed the Internet a little.  Looks like the only place I have found (that isn't charging outrageous rates...$100 a night at the Frankenmuth Super8?? come-on!!!) is the Saginaw/Frankenmuth Red Roof Inn about 13 miles up the road from where the host hotel is (the Birch Run/Frankenmuth Best Western).  It's roughly $50 a night at the Red Roof Inn.  I went ahead and made a preliminary reservation just in case I can't find anything better. <P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rodney||06-16-2001||08:22 AM||||I have a room at the host hotel for Friday night only. It is very possible I'll be looking for a room mate for just Friday night. ||||reg||1
